Z||000009||Raydar||07-14-2000||04:37 PM||||When reading this, keep in mind that I'm an older fart. I don't go in for a lot of stripes and "big" graphics. Bright colors are cool...<BR>I like the Grand Sport blue, as well. I would leave off the little stripes that they put over the wheel well. I understand the reason that they were put on the race car, but I think they spoil the looks of the car. <BR>As for emblems, etc. Look at the later style "FORMULA" decals, from the 91-92 Firebird. They are really uncommon, but they will still be original Pontiac. Or, you could use the small Firebird Formula bumper decals from the 88-89 model. Put them on the ends of the wing. They look like they'd fit just about right. <P>On the outside chance that you actually use this, I'll call it "Kozmic Blue" -from a Janis Joplin album.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>------------------<P>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||07-14-2000||04:50 PM||||good suggestions.......I like the formula decal on the wing idea!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pontiaddict||07-14-2000||06:14 PM||||I think the color's Admiralty blue. For the stripe, go with a light gray. I'll try and do  a picture!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fret Naught||07-14-2000||07:35 PM||||I would go with a solid color, then just behind the front wheels, diagonaly up over the rear wheels put some type of Zig Zag graphic in a complementing color or even two colors.||||reg||1
Z||000013||BAM-BAM||07-14-2000||07:41 PM||||  Formula, try this. How about silver, like the newer lexus's. Now, add a ghost stripe in black or even a double ghost stripe scheme. last, have the FORMULA on the doors and decklid airbrushed in the same ghost color as the stripes. I think that would really bring out the lines of your car accented by the black Formula wheels. Just a thought. Then you could name it the "SILVER BULLET". Have fun and good luck.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> P.S. Now, imagine if you used a pearl addative  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000014||Formula||07-14-2000||08:15 PM||||Bam, What exactly is a ghost stripe????  It definetly sounds like a cool idea too....I'll look into this one too.<P>Fret, could you draw (or find a pic) of the zig zag idea your talking about.  I cant seem to picture what your saying.<P>One of my friends said to paint it Dark Red Met. and put the Viper stripes on it and have a stripe slant down over the back wheel and go down near where it says Formula now, and go straight to the front wheel.  This seems interesting to, I would probably get Formula writen Black on the side stripe.<P>I plan on switching my tailight covers over to the same color as the stripe too...<P>I still havent decided on the designs/colors yet.  I'm kind of glad that someone painted all of the door jams and under the hood and deck black, it will make a color change really easy!!||||reg||1
