Z||000021||Taijiguy||07-14-2000||10:16 PM||||I'm painting mine gun-metal grey metallic, with pearl white striping, so I'm not going to suggest that one. However, I'll pass on my first idea, with different colors. Since you seem to like the blue, how about the blue, with 70's Z-28 striping in gold (or white) The Z-28 had the two stripes that started a few inches back from the edge of the hood, ran up to the cowling, and then picked up again on the deck lid, (skipping the roof) stopping a few inches from the back edge of the trunk. The starting point on the hood, and the ending point on the deck lid were rounded on the corners, and sported a 1/4" pinstrip outline on both stripes. Totally awsome look. I also thought about the SS nose stripe, that ran up the fender in front of the wheel openings, went across the hood and down the other side. I loved those graphics from back then.....<BR>Of course, then there's the Starsky & Hutch stripe......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>This is similar to the Z-28 striping  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002922.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002922.html</A>  Only I wouldn't start them on the nose, but back on the hood, and I wouldn't run them over the spoiler.<P>Taiji<p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 07-14-2000).]||||reg||1
