Z||000024||My7Fieros||07-14-2000||11:15 PM||||How about keeping it the way it is? I like it. Sorry, Im just personally not into flashy neon colors and wild graphix on cars...too "ricey" for me. Im kind of a "keep it pretty much the way they made it at the factory" kinda guy. I just think if you paint it a neon puke green with wild stickers all over it, in a years time (at most) you'll grow seriously sick of it. You can only paint a car so many times before you have to remove all the paint down to the base color and start over. But, to each his own.||||reg||9
Z||000025||webbee||07-14-2000||11:32 PM||||I like the blue w/graphic or blue w/stripe but not together.<P>Look at Lowrider or back issues of Hot Rod there are some great paint jobs out there that can be adapted to the Fiero.<P>Your public library might be a resource for back issues.<P>If the body isn't wavy, I LOVE black especially w/pearl in it 	||||reg||10
Z||000026||BAM-BAM||07-14-2000||11:49 PM||||Formula, a ghost stripe or ghost flame is a stripe or flame that is barely discernable. In other words, you can barely make it out untill you are right on top of it. Even then it remains slight to the eye. It is a very cool touch to a custom paint job, especially if it is pearalized. You can pick just about any color for the ghost, I just suggested black to catch the wheels. I am planning something similar when I paint but more than likely it will be in the red or yellow vein. That way  it will pick up the center caps on the wheels I am going to get and also compliment the stitching in my interior leather. I really did like the Graphics on the red GT also. If you have any more questions, just E-Mail me Bartlettds@lvcm.com .<P>  Late BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
